IMPORT prelude

-- Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA) -- discrimination, harassment and victimisation in work, from the seat of the
-- employee or job applicant.
--
-- SEAT: the employee, or the person applying for a job, who says an employer discriminated against them, that someone
-- harassed them sexually or racially at work, or that they were victimised for using the Act. "Is this
-- discrimination as the Act defines it?", "Was what my employer did unlawful?", "Does an exception let my employer do
-- it?", "Was I sexually or racially harassed, unlawfully?", "Was I victimised?", "Is my employer answerable for what a
-- fellow employee did?". The employer, the harasser and the victimiser are the persons the Act binds; no seat is
-- written for them. The Commissioner and the State Administrative Tribunal get no seat: their decisions are facts.
--
-- Every exported question takes plain facts (yes/no, a number, a choice from a list). Judgments the Act leaves to
-- someone else ("not reasonable having regard to the circumstances", "reasonable grounds for believing", "a genuine
-- occupational qualification", "unjustifiable hardship", "in good faith") are INPUTS, never decided here. Under s 123
-- the respondent must prove an exception: an exception input means "the employer has shown that ...".
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 4(1) (employment, family responsibility or family status, gender reassigned person, impairment,
-- race), s 5; the meaning of discrimination in ss 8, 9, 10, 10A, 35AB, 35A, 35O, 36, 53, 66A, 66V(1), (3), 67A; the
-- employer's duties to applicants and employees in ss 11, 35AC, 35B, 35P, 37, 54, 66B, 66W, 67B; the work exceptions in
-- ss 11(3), 27, 28, 29, 31, 33, 35AC(3), 35B(3), (4), 35K, 35M, 35P(3), 35ZD, 37(3), 50, 51, 54(4), 66, 66B(3), 66Q(1),
-- (2), 66R, 66S, 66W(3), 66ZM, 66ZN(1), 66ZP, 66ZQ, 66ZS(1); sexual harassment in employment (s 24(1), (3), (4)); racial
-- harassment in employment (ss 49A(1), (3), 49D); victimisation (s 67); the general exceptions in ss 69, 72, 73(1);
-- liability (ss 160, 161). Out, with reasons, in NOTES.md.
--
-- Edition: Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA), compilation retrieved 7 September 2026 from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc
-- 48472), whose compilation table ends with the Industrial Relations Legislation Amendment Act 2024 (No. 43 of 2024, in
-- operation 31 January 2025); deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48472.txt.
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website, State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. Answers follow the rulings on negatives of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05
-- (NOTES.md): an answer that is the text's own no says "(the text's no)"; an answer where the text is limited by its own
-- wording or silent is marked "NOTHING-kind".

§ `Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA): discrimination, harassment and victimisation in work`

§§ `The grounds and what was done`

-- The grounds of Parts II to IVC. Religious and political conviction share s 53 and s 54, but s 54(3) and s 66(2) treat
-- them apart, so they are listed apart.
DECLARE `Ground` IS ONE OF
    `sex`
    `marital status`
    `pregnancy`
    `breast feeding or bottle feeding`
    `gender history`
    `family responsibility or family status`
    `sexual orientation`
    `race`
    `religious conviction`
    `political conviction`
    `impairment`
    `age`
    `publication of my details on the Fines Enforcement Registrar website`

-- What the employer did, in the words of s 11(1), (2) (repeated in ss 35AC, 35B, 35P, 37, 54, 66B, 66W, 67B) and
-- s 54(3). "employment" includes part-time and temporary employment, work under a contract for services and work as a
-- State employee (s 4(1)).
DECLARE `What was done` IS ONE OF
    `in the arrangements made for deciding who should be offered employment`
    `in deciding who should be offered employment`
    `in the terms or conditions on which employment was offered`
    `in the terms or conditions of my employment`
    `by denying or limiting my access to promotion, transfer, training or other benefits of employment`
    `by dismissing me`
    `by subjecting me to any other detriment`
    `by refusing me permission to carry out a religious practice during working hours`

GIVEN w IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A STRING
`the paragraph for` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `in the arrangements made for deciding who should be offered employment` THEN "(1)(a)"
    WHEN `in deciding who should be offered employment` THEN "(1)(b)"
    WHEN `in the terms or conditions on which employment was offered` THEN "(1)(c)"
    WHEN `in the terms or conditions of my employment` THEN "(2)(a)"
    WHEN `by denying or limiting my access to promotion, transfer, training or other benefits of employment` THEN "(2)(b)"
    WHEN `by dismissing me` THEN "(2)(c)"
    WHEN `by subjecting me to any other detriment` THEN "(2)(d)"
    WHEN `by refusing me permission to carry out a religious practice during working hours` THEN "(3)"

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`
GIVETH A STRING
`the work section for` g MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `gender history` THEN "s 35AC"
    WHEN `family responsibility or family status` THEN "s 35B"
    WHEN `sexual orientation` THEN "s 35P"
    WHEN `race` THEN "s 37"
    WHEN `religious conviction` THEN "s 54"
    WHEN `political conviction` THEN "s 54"
    WHEN `impairment` THEN "s 66B"
    WHEN `age` THEN "s 66W"
    WHEN `publication of my details on the Fines Enforcement Registrar website` THEN "s 67B"
    OTHERWISE "s 11"

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`
GIVETH A STRING
`the meaning section for` g MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `sex` THEN "s 8"
    WHEN `marital status` THEN "s 9"
    WHEN `pregnancy` THEN "s 10"
    WHEN `breast feeding or bottle feeding` THEN "s 10A"
    WHEN `gender history` THEN "s 35AB"
    WHEN `family responsibility or family status` THEN "s 35A"
    WHEN `sexual orientation` THEN "s 35O"
    WHEN `race` THEN "s 36"
    WHEN `religious conviction` THEN "s 53"
    WHEN `political conviction` THEN "s 53"
    WHEN `impairment` THEN "s 66A"
    WHEN `age` THEN "s 66V"
    WHEN `publication of my details on the Fines Enforcement Registrar website` THEN "s 67A"

-- Applying for a job: s 11(1) and its fellows. Employed: s 11(2) and its fellows.
GIVEN w IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it was done to me as an applicant` w IF
        w EQUALS `in the arrangements made for deciding who should be offered employment`
    OR  w EQUALS `in deciding who should be offered employment`
    OR  w EQUALS `in the terms or conditions on which employment was offered`

-- s 11(1)(a) or (b): the arrangements, or the decision, about who should be offered employment.
GIVEN w IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it was the choice of whom to employ` w IF
        w EQUALS `in the arrangements made for deciding who should be offered employment`
    OR  w EQUALS `in deciding who should be offered employment`

§§ `s 4(1) -- the Act's own terms`

-- s 4(1): "gender reassigned person means -- (a) a person who has been issued with a recognition certificate under the
-- Gender Reassignment Act 2000 or a certificate that was an equivalent certificate for the purposes of that Act; or (b)
-- a person -- (i) whose sex or gender in the registration of the person's birth under the Births, Deaths and Marriages
-- Registration Act 1998 has been changed under section 36Q of that Act; or (ii) who has been issued a document
-- acknowledging the person's sex or gender under the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 section 36ZA".
-- Paragraph (b) came with No. 31 of 2024 (in operation 30 May 2025). The certificates and the register entries are
-- borrowed: asked as facts. A "means" definition: outside it, the text's no.
DECLARE `Am I a gender reassigned person` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I hold a recognition certificate or an equivalent certificate (s 4(1), paragraph (a))`
    `yes: the sex or gender in my birth registration has been changed under s 36Q of the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (s 4(1), paragraph (b)(i))`
    `yes: I have been issued a document acknowledging my sex or gender under s 36ZA of the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (s 4(1), paragraph (b)(ii))`
    `no: a gender reassigned person means only a person with one of those certificates, changes or documents (a "means" definition: the text's no)`

@export Am I a "gender reassigned person", the only person Part IIAA of the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA) protects from discrimination on gender history grounds (s 4(1))? Since 30 May 2025 this includes a person whose birth registration was changed under s 36Q, or who holds a document under s 36ZA, of the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998.
GIVEN `I hold a recognition certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been issued a recognition certificate under the Gender Reassignment Act 2000, or a certificate that was an equivalent certificate for that Act?
      `my birth registration was changed under s 36Q` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sex or gender in the registration of your birth under the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 been changed under section 36Q of that Act?
      `I hold a s 36ZA document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been issued a document acknowledging your sex or gender under section 36ZA of the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998?
GIVETH AN `Am I a gender reassigned person`
`s 4 -- am I a gender reassigned person` `I hold a recognition certificate` `my birth registration was changed under s 36Q` `I hold a s 36ZA document` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I hold a recognition certificate` THEN `yes: I hold a recognition certificate or an equivalent certificate (s 4(1), paragraph (a))`
        IF `my birth registration was changed under s 36Q` THEN `yes: the sex or gender in my birth registration has been changed under s 36Q of the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (s 4(1), paragraph (b)(i))`
        IF `I hold a s 36ZA document` THEN `yes: I have been issued a document acknowledging my sex or gender under s 36ZA of the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998 (s 4(1), paragraph (b)(ii))`
        OTHERWISE `no: a gender reassigned person means only a person with one of those certificates, changes or documents (a "means" definition: the text's no)`

-- s 4(1): "impairment in relation to a person, means one or more of the following conditions -- (a) any defect or
-- disturbance in the normal structure or functioning of a person's body; or (b) any defect or disturbance in the normal
-- structure or functioning of a person's brain; or (c) any illness or condition which impairs a person's thought
-- processes, perception of reality, emotions or judgment or which results in disturbed behaviour, whether arising from a
-- condition subsisting at birth or from an illness or injury and includes an impairment -- (d) which presently exists or
-- existed in the past but has now ceased to exist; or (e) which is imputed to the person". A "means" definition, widened
-- by "includes" (d) and (e).
DECLARE `Do I have an impairment` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I have, or had in the past, an impairment as s 4(1) defines it`
    `yes: an impairment is imputed to me (s 4(1), paragraph (e))`
    `no: none of the conditions in s 4(1) (a) to (c) is present, past or imputed (a "means" definition: the text's no)`

@export Do I have an "impairment" for the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA) (s 4(1))? It means a defect or disturbance of the body or brain, or an illness or condition affecting thought, perception, emotions or judgment or causing disturbed behaviour, from birth, illness or injury; it includes one you had in the past and one people think you have.
GIVEN `a defect or disturbance of my body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have, or did you have in the past, a defect or disturbance in the normal structure or functioning of your body?
      `a defect or disturbance of my brain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have, or did you have in the past, a defect or disturbance in the normal structure or functioning of your brain?
      `an illness affecting my mind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have, or did you have in the past, an illness or condition that impairs your thought processes, perception of reality, emotions or judgment, or that results in disturbed behaviour?
      `one is imputed to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is such a condition imputed to you (people treat you as having one), whether or not you have it?
GIVETH A `Do I have an impairment`
`s 4 -- do I have an impairment` `a defect or disturbance of my body` `a defect or disturbance of my brain` `an illness affecting my mind` `one is imputed to me` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a defect or disturbance of my body` OR `a defect or disturbance of my brain` OR `an illness affecting my mind`
        THEN `yes: I have, or had in the past, an impairment as s 4(1) defines it`
        IF `one is imputed to me` THEN `yes: an impairment is imputed to me (s 4(1), paragraph (e))`
        OTHERWISE `no: none of the conditions in s 4(1) (a) to (c) is present, past or imputed (a "means" definition: the text's no)`

-- s 4(1): "family responsibility or family status, in relation to a person, means -- (a) having responsibility for the
-- care of another person, whether or not that person is a dependant, other than in the course of paid employment; or
-- (b) the status of being a particular relative; or (c) the status of being a relative of a particular person".
-- "relative ... means a person who is related to the firstmentioned person by blood, marriage, affinity or adoption and
-- includes a person who is wholly or mainly dependent on, or is a member of the household of, the firstmentioned person".
DECLARE `Do I have a family responsibility or family status` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I have responsibility for the care of another person, other than in paid employment (s 4(1), paragraph (a))`
    `yes: I have the status of being a particular relative, or a relative of a particular person (s 4(1), paragraphs (b) and (c))`
    `no: caring only in the course of paid employment, and no relative status, is outside the definition (a "means" definition: the text's no)`

@export Do I have a "family responsibility or family status" for the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA) (s 4(1))? It means caring for another person (not as paid work), being a particular relative (a parent, a spouse), or being the relative of a particular person.
GIVEN `I care for another person, not as paid work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have responsibility for the care of another person (whether or not they depend on you), other than in the course of paid employment?
      `the matter is my being a relative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter your status of being a particular relative (for example a parent or a spouse), or of being the relative of a particular person? A relative is related by blood, marriage, affinity or adoption, or is wholly or mainly dependent on you or a member of your household.
GIVETH A `Do I have a family responsibility or family status`
`s 4 -- do I have a family responsibility or family status` `I care for another person, not as paid work` `the matter is my being a relative` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I care for another person, not as paid work` THEN `yes: I have responsibility for the care of another person, other than in paid employment (s 4(1), paragraph (a))`
        IF `the matter is my being a relative` THEN `yes: I have the status of being a particular relative, or a relative of a particular person (s 4(1), paragraphs (b) and (c))`
        OTHERWISE `no: caring only in the course of paid employment, and no relative status, is outside the definition (a "means" definition: the text's no)`

§§ `ss 5, 8 to 67A -- Is it discrimination as the Act defines it?`

-- The facts of the treatment, as the person can state them. Each definition (ss 8 to 67A) has a direct limb (less
-- favourable treatment "on the ground of" the attribute, or a characteristic that appertains generally to, or is
-- generally imputed to, persons with it) and an indirect limb (a requirement or condition). s 5: the ground need not be
-- the dominant or substantial reason, so "one of the reasons" is enough.
DECLARE `The treatment` HAS
    `treated less favourably because of my attribute` IS A BOOLEAN
    `treated less favourably because of an associate's attribute` IS A BOOLEAN
    `segregated because of race` IS A BOOLEAN
    `treated as being of my former sex` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the less favourable treatment was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a guide dog or hearing dog` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a requirement or condition was imposed on me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a substantially higher proportion of others comply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the requirement is not reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I do not or cannot comply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a gender reassigned person` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Is it discrimination` IS ONE OF
    `discrimination` HAS `the kind` IS A STRING, `the provision` IS A STRING
    `not discrimination as the Act defines it for this ground (the definition's "if" is not met: the text's no)`
    `NOTHING-kind: Part IIAA reaches only a gender reassigned person; the Act does not say what else applies`

-- The three limbs of the indirect test, common to ss 8(2), 9(2), 10(2), 10A(2), 35A(2), 35AB(3)(b), 35O(3), 36(2),
-- 53(2), 66A(3), 66V(3): "(a) with which a substantially higher proportion of persons [without the attribute] comply or
-- are able to comply; and (b) which is not reasonable having regard to the circumstances of the case; and (c) with which
-- the aggrieved person does not or is not able to comply." s 67A(b) asks only that the requirement be "not reasonable".
GIVEN t IS A `The treatment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the three-limb requirement test is met` t IF
        t's `a requirement or condition was imposed on me`
    AND t's `a substantially higher proportion of others comply`
    AND t's `the requirement is not reasonable`
    AND t's `I do not or cannot comply`

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`
GIVETH A STRING
`the indirect subsection for` g MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `gender history` THEN "(3)(b)"
    WHEN `sexual orientation` THEN "(3)"
    WHEN `impairment` THEN "(3)"
    WHEN `age` THEN "(3)"
    WHEN `publication of my details on the Fines Enforcement Registrar website` THEN "(b)"
    OTHERWISE "(2)"

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`
GIVETH A STRING
`the direct subsection for` g MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `publication of my details on the Fines Enforcement Registrar website` THEN "(a)"
    OTHERWISE "(1)"

-- The relative-or-associate limbs exist for three grounds only: s 35O(2) (sexual orientation), s 36(1a) (race), s 66A(1a)
-- (impairment). s 66V(2) (age) is "for the purposes of sections 66ZE, 66ZF and 66ZG" (other areas, not work) and is not
-- used here.
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`
GIVETH A STRING
`the associate subsection for` g MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `sexual orientation` THEN "(2)"
    WHEN `race` THEN "(1a)"
    WHEN `impairment` THEN "(1a)"
    OTHERWISE ""

`the associate kind` MEANS "through a relative or associate: less favourable treatment because of their attribute"

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, t IS A `The treatment`
GIVETH AN `Is it discrimination`
`the meaning of discrimination` g t MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF g EQUALS `gender history` AND (NOT (t's `I am a gender reassigned person`))
        THEN `NOTHING-kind: Part IIAA reaches only a gender reassigned person; the Act does not say what else applies`
        -- s 10(1)(b): for pregnancy the less favourable treatment must also be "not reasonable in the circumstances".
        IF      t's `treated less favourably because of my attribute`
            AND (NOT (g EQUALS `pregnancy` AND t's `the less favourable treatment was reasonable`))
        THEN `discrimination` "direct: less favourable treatment on the ground" (CONCAT (`the meaning section for` g), (`the direct subsection for` g))
        -- s 35AB(3)(a): treating a gender reassigned person "as being of the person's former sex".
        IF g EQUALS `gender history` AND t's `treated as being of my former sex`
        THEN `discrimination` "direct: treated as being of the former sex" "s 35AB(3)(a)"
        -- s 36(1)(e): segregating the person from persons of a different race (and s 36(1a)(e) for a relative's race).
        IF g EQUALS `race` AND t's `segregated because of race`
        THEN `discrimination` "direct: segregation on the ground of race" "s 36(1)(e) or (1a)(e)"
        -- s 66A(4): a person who is blind, deaf, partially blind or partially deaf treated less favourably because of a
        -- guide dog or hearing dog (fork F4).
        IF g EQUALS `impairment` AND t's `a guide dog or hearing dog`
        THEN `discrimination` "direct: less favourable treatment because of a guide dog or hearing dog" "s 66A(4)"
        IF      g EQUALS `publication of my details on the Fines Enforcement Registrar website`
            AND t's `a requirement or condition was imposed on me`
            AND t's `the requirement is not reasonable`
        THEN `discrimination` "indirect: a requirement or condition that is not reasonable" "s 67A(b)"
        IF      (NOT (g EQUALS `publication of my details on the Fines Enforcement Registrar website`))
            AND `the three-limb requirement test is met` t
        THEN `discrimination` "indirect: a requirement or condition" (CONCAT (`the meaning section for` g), (`the indirect subsection for` g))
        IF      (NOT (`the associate subsection for` g EQUALS ""))
            AND t's `treated less favourably because of an associate's attribute`
        THEN `discrimination` `the associate kind` (CONCAT (`the meaning section for` g), (`the associate subsection for` g))
        OTHERWISE `not discrimination as the Act defines it for this ground (the definition's "if" is not met: the text's no)`

@export Was I "discriminated against", as the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA) defines it, on the ground of my sex, marital status, pregnancy, breast feeding, gender history, family responsibility, sexual orientation, race, religious or political conviction, impairment, age, or the publication of my details on the Fines Enforcement Registrar's website (ss 5, 8 to 10A, 35A, 35AB, 35O, 36, 53, 66A, 66V, 67A)? Direct: you were treated less favourably than someone without your attribute in the same circumstances, because of it. Indirect: you had to meet an unreasonable requirement that people without your attribute meet more easily, and you could not.
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Ground` @desc The attribute you say you were treated badly for. One of: sex; marital status; pregnancy; breast feeding or bottle feeding; gender history; family responsibility or family status; sexual orientation; race (including colour, descent, ethnic or national origin or nationality); religious conviction; political conviction; impairment; age; publication of my details on the Fines Enforcement Registrar website
      `treated less favourably because of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you treated less favourably than a person without that attribute would be treated in the same or not materially different circumstances, because of your attribute or a characteristic generally belonging to or generally imputed to people with it (for impairment, also because you need a palliative device)? It is enough that this was one of the reasons
      `treated less favourably because of an associate's attribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you treated less favourably because of the attribute of a relative or associate of yours (the Act defines this for sexual orientation, race and impairment)?
      `segregated because of race` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For race only: were you segregated from people of a different race because of your race, or a relative's or associate's race?
      `treated as being of my former sex` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For gender history only: were you treated as being of your former sex because you have a gender history?
      `the less favourable treatment was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For pregnancy only: has it been found that the less favourable treatment was reasonable in the circumstances?
      `a guide dog or hearing dog` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For impairment only: are you blind, deaf, partially blind or partially deaf, and were you treated less favourably because you have or are accompanied by a guide dog or hearing dog (or something related to that)?
      `a requirement or condition was imposed on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you required to comply with a requirement or condition (a rule, policy or practice)?
      `a substantially higher proportion of others comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do a substantially higher proportion of people without your attribute comply, or are they able to comply, with that requirement or condition?
      `the requirement is not reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement or condition not reasonable having regard to the circumstances of the case (a judgment for the Tribunal: answer as found, or as you put it)?
      `I do not or cannot comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you not comply, or are you not able to comply, with the requirement or condition?
      `I am a gender reassigned person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For gender history only: are you a gender reassigned person (a recognition certificate, a birth registration changed under s 36Q, or a document under s 36ZA of the Births, Deaths and Marriages Registration Act 1998)?
GIVETH AN `Is it discrimination`
`ss 8 to 67A -- was I discriminated against` `the ground` `treated less favourably because of it` `treated less favourably because of an associate's attribute` `segregated because of race` `treated as being of my former sex` `the less favourable treatment was reasonable` `a guide dog or hearing dog` `a requirement or condition was imposed on me` `a substantially higher proportion of others comply` `the requirement is not reasonable` `I do not or cannot comply` `I am a gender reassigned person` MEANS
    `the meaning of discrimination` `the ground` (`The treatment` WITH
        `treated less favourably because of my attribute` IS `treated less favourably because of it`
        `treated less favourably because of an associate's attribute` IS `treated less favourably because of an associate's attribute`
        `segregated because of race` IS `segregated because of race`
        `treated as being of my former sex` IS `treated as being of my former sex`
        `the less favourable treatment was reasonable` IS `the less favourable treatment was reasonable`
        `a guide dog or hearing dog` IS `a guide dog or hearing dog`
        `a requirement or condition was imposed on me` IS `a requirement or condition was imposed on me`
        `a substantially higher proportion of others comply` IS `a substantially higher proportion of others comply`
        `the requirement is not reasonable` IS `the requirement is not reasonable`
        `I do not or cannot comply` IS `I do not or cannot comply`
        `I am a gender reassigned person` IS `I am a gender reassigned person`)

§§ `ss 11, 35AC, 35B, 35P, 37, 54, 66B, 66W, 67B and their exceptions -- Was what my employer did unlawful?`

-- The facts an exception turns on. Under s 123 the employer (the respondent) must prove an exception, so each means
-- "the employer has shown that ...". Judgments in them ("genuine occupational qualification", "reasonable",
-- "unjustifiable hardship", "in good faith") are the Tribunal's, asked as found.
DECLARE `The exception facts` HAS
    `domestic duties where the employer lives` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer's number of employees` IS A NUMBER
    `being of the other sex is a genuine occupational qualification` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer already has enough employees of the other sex for the duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `only rights given to women for pregnancy, childbirth or feeding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the job is one of two for a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a measure for equal opportunity or special needs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the duties involve caring for children where they live` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my spouse is meant to work for the employer too` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a likelihood of collusion with my relative` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the work needs a particular race, impairment or age for authenticity or welfare services` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a religious school or religious health service, and religious duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a political job` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employer reasonably concluded I could not do the work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the terms are reasonable given my impairment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `terms imposed for reasonable health and safety considerations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an offer of a voluntary retirement or severance scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `necessary to comply with a youth wages provision or an older written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `necessary to comply with an order of the Tribunal or a court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a religious appointment or a religious body's practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `staff of a religious school, in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The facts of s 54(3): a religious practice "(a) of a kind recognised as necessary or desirable by persons of the same
-- religious conviction as that of the employee; and (b) the performance of which during working hours is reasonable
-- having regard to the circumstances of the employment; and (c) that does not subject the employer to any detriment."
DECLARE `The religious practice` HAS
    `recognised as necessary or desirable by my religion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonable to do in working hours` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no detriment to the employer` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The first exception that applies, in the order of the Act; NOTHING if none does.
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, w IS A `What was done`, e IS A `The exception facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the work exception for` g w e MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- The domestic-duties exceptions differ by ground in what they cover (finding 3).
        IF g EQUALS `sex` AND `it was the choice of whom to employ` w AND e's `domestic duties where the employer lives`
        THEN JUST "s 11(3): domestic duties on the premises where the employer resides (choice of whom to employ only)"
        IF g EQUALS `gender history` AND e's `domestic duties where the employer lives`
        THEN JUST "s 35AC(3): domestic duties within a private household in which the employer resides"
        IF g EQUALS `family responsibility or family status` AND `it was done to me as an applicant` w AND e's `domestic duties where the employer lives`
        THEN JUST "s 35B(3): domestic duties within a private household in which the employer resides (applicants only)"
        IF g EQUALS `sexual orientation` AND `it was the choice of whom to employ` w AND e's `domestic duties where the employer lives`
        THEN JUST "s 35P(3): domestic duties on the premises where the employer resides (choice of whom to employ only)"
        IF g EQUALS `race` AND `it was done to me as an applicant` w AND e's `domestic duties where the employer lives`
        THEN JUST "s 37(3): domestic duties within a private household in which the employer resides (applicants only)"
        IF (g EQUALS `religious conviction` OR g EQUALS `political conviction`) AND e's `domestic duties where the employer lives`
        THEN JUST "s 54(4)(a): domestic duties on the premises where the employer resides"
        IF (g EQUALS `religious conviction` OR g EQUALS `political conviction`) AND e's `the employer's number of employees` AT MOST 5
        THEN JUST "s 54(4)(b): the employer employs no more than 5 persons, not counting domestic workers"
        IF g EQUALS `impairment` AND `it was done to me as an applicant` w AND e's `domestic duties where the employer lives`
        THEN JUST "s 66B(3): domestic duties on the premises where the employer resides (applicants only)"
        IF g EQUALS `age` AND `it was done to me as an applicant` w AND e's `domestic duties where the employer lives`
        THEN JUST "s 66W(3): domestic duties within a private household in which the employer resides (applicants only)"
        -- s 27: a genuine occupational qualification to be of the other sex, for s 11(1)(a) or (b), unless s 27(3) (the
        -- employer already has enough capable employees of that sex whom it would be reasonable to put on the duties).
        IF      g EQUALS `sex` AND `it was the choice of whom to employ` w
            AND e's `being of the other sex is a genuine occupational qualification`
            AND (NOT (e's `the employer already has enough employees of the other sex for the duties`))
        THEN JUST "s 27: being of the other sex is a genuine occupational qualification for the position"
        IF g EQUALS `sex` AND e's `only rights given to women for pregnancy, childbirth or feeding`
        THEN JUST "s 28: rights or privileges granted to women in connection with pregnancy, childbirth, breast feeding or bottle feeding"
        IF g EQUALS `marital status` AND e's `the job is one of two for a couple`
        THEN JUST "s 29: a job which is one of 2 to be held by a married couple or de facto partners"
        IF      (g EQUALS `sex` OR g EQUALS `marital status` OR g EQUALS `pregnancy` OR g EQUALS `breast feeding or bottle feeding`)
            AND e's `a measure for equal opportunity or special needs`
        THEN JUST "s 31: a measure intended to achieve equality"
        IF g EQUALS `family responsibility or family status` AND e's `a measure for equal opportunity or special needs`
        THEN JUST "s 35B(4) and s 35K: rights, benefits or privileges, or a measure to meet special needs, for persons with a family responsibility or family status"
        IF g EQUALS `sexual orientation` AND e's `a measure for equal opportunity or special needs`
        THEN JUST "s 35ZD: a measure intended to achieve equality"
        IF g EQUALS `race` AND e's `a measure for equal opportunity or special needs`
        THEN JUST "s 51: a measure intended to achieve equality"
        IF g EQUALS `impairment` AND e's `a measure for equal opportunity or special needs`
        THEN JUST "s 66R: a measure intended to achieve equality"
        IF g EQUALS `age` AND e's `a measure for equal opportunity or special needs`
        THEN JUST "s 66ZP: a measure intended to achieve equality"
        IF g EQUALS `sex` AND `it was the choice of whom to employ` w AND e's `the duties involve caring for children where they live`
        THEN JUST "s 33(1): residential care of children"
        IF      g EQUALS `marital status`
            AND (`it was the choice of whom to employ` w OR w EQUALS `by dismissing me`)
            AND e's `the duties involve caring for children where they live`
            AND e's `my spouse is meant to work for the employer too`
        THEN JUST "s 33(2): residential care of children, where the occupant's spouse is also to be employed"
        IF g EQUALS `family responsibility or family status` AND e's `a likelihood of collusion with my relative`
        THEN JUST "s 35M: a demonstrated significant likelihood of collusion with a relative, damaging the employer's business"
        IF g EQUALS `race` AND e's `the work needs a particular race, impairment or age for authenticity or welfare services`
        THEN JUST "s 50: genuine occupational qualification (authenticity, or welfare services best given by a person of the same race)"
        IF (g EQUALS `religious conviction` OR g EQUALS `political conviction`) AND e's `a religious school or religious health service, and religious duties`
        THEN JUST "s 66(1): a private educational authority, or a religious body in a health service, where the duties involve religious observance or practice"
        IF g EQUALS `political conviction` AND `it was done to me as an applicant` w AND e's `a political job`
        THEN JUST "s 66(2): offering a political job (electoral officer, ministerial adviser, party worker, electoral staff)"
        IF      g EQUALS `impairment`
            AND (w EQUALS `in deciding who should be offered employment` OR w EQUALS `by dismissing me`)
            AND e's `the employer reasonably concluded I could not do the work`
        THEN JUST "s 66Q(1): reasonable to conclude the person could not do the work reasonably required, or would need services or facilities imposing unjustifiable hardship"
        IF      g EQUALS `impairment`
            AND (   w EQUALS `in the terms or conditions on which employment was offered`
                 OR w EQUALS `in the terms or conditions of my employment`
                 OR w EQUALS `by denying or limiting my access to promotion, transfer, training or other benefits of employment`)
            AND e's `the terms are reasonable given my impairment`
        THEN JUST "s 66Q(2): terms or conditions reasonable having regard to the limitation the impairment imposes, or the services or facilities needed"
        IF g EQUALS `impairment` AND e's `the work needs a particular race, impairment or age for authenticity or welfare services`
        THEN JUST "s 66S: genuine occupational qualification (authenticity, or welfare services best given by a person with the same impairment)"
        IF      g EQUALS `age`
            AND (w EQUALS `in the terms or conditions on which employment was offered` OR w EQUALS `in the terms or conditions of my employment`)
            AND e's `terms imposed for reasonable health and safety considerations`
        THEN JUST "s 66ZM: terms and conditions imposed to comply with reasonable health and safety considerations"
        IF g EQUALS `age` AND e's `an offer of a voluntary retirement or severance scheme`
        THEN JUST "s 66ZN(1): an offer of a voluntary retirement, retirement incentive, severance or like scheme"
        IF g EQUALS `age` AND e's `the work needs a particular race, impairment or age for authenticity or welfare services`
        THEN JUST "s 66ZQ: genuine occupational qualification (authenticity, or welfare services best given by a person of a particular age)"
        IF g EQUALS `age` AND e's `necessary to comply with a youth wages provision or an older written law`
        THEN JUST "s 66ZS(1): necessary to comply with a youth wages or ratio provision of an award, agreement or the Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993, or a written law in force when Part IVB began"
        IF e's `necessary to comply with an order of the Tribunal or a court`
        THEN JUST "s 69: necessary to comply with an order of the Tribunal or of a court"
        IF e's `a religious appointment or a religious body's practice`
        THEN JUST "s 72: religious appointments, or an act of a religious body conforming to its doctrines or avoiding injury to adherents' religious susceptibilities"
        IF e's `staff of a religious school, in good faith`
        THEN JUST "s 73(1): staff of a religious educational institution, in good faith to avoid injury to adherents' religious susceptibilities"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `Was it unlawful in work` IS ONE OF
    `unlawful` HAS `the provision broken` IS A STRING, `the meaning of discrimination used` IS A STRING
    `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` HAS `the exception` IS A STRING
    `not unlawful: not discrimination as the Act defines it for this ground (the text's no)`
    `not unlawful under s 54(3): the practice is not one the subsection protects (the text's no)`
    `NOTHING-kind` HAS `why` IS A STRING

GIVEN `the exception` IS A MAYBE STRING, `the provision` IS A STRING, `the meaning` IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Was it unlawful in work`
`unless an exception applies` `the exception` `the provision` `the meaning` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the exception`
    WHEN JUST x THEN `not unlawful: an exception applies (the text's no)` x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `unlawful` `the provision` `the meaning`

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, w IS A `What was done`, d IS AN `Is it discrimination`, e IS A `The exception facts`
GIVETH A `Was it unlawful in work`
`the work answer for discrimination` g w d e MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `NOTHING-kind: Part IIAA reaches only a gender reassigned person; the Act does not say what else applies`
        THEN `NOTHING-kind` "s 35AC protects only a gender reassigned person (s 4(1)); whether other law reaches this is outside this Act"
    WHEN `not discrimination as the Act defines it for this ground (the definition's "if" is not met: the text's no)`
        THEN `not unlawful: not discrimination as the Act defines it for this ground (the text's no)`
    WHEN `discrimination` k p THEN
        IF k EQUALS `the associate kind`
        THEN `NOTHING-kind` (CONCAT (`the work section for` g), " forbids discrimination on the ground of the person's own attribute; whether discrimination through a relative or associate falls within it is not said (fork F3)")
        ELSE `unless an exception applies` (`the work exception for` g w e) (CONCAT (`the work section for` g), (`the paragraph for` w)) p

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, w IS A `What was done`, t IS A `The treatment`, e IS A `The exception facts`, r IS A `The religious practice`
GIVETH A `Was it unlawful in work`
`the work answer` g w t e r MEANS
    IF w EQUALS `by refusing me permission to carry out a religious practice during working hours`
    THEN IF (NOT (g EQUALS `religious conviction`))
         THEN `NOTHING-kind` "s 54(3) is about refusing a religious practice on the ground of religious conviction; choose another thing done for this ground"
         ELSE IF     r's `recognised as necessary or desirable by my religion`
                 AND r's `reasonable to do in working hours`
                 AND r's `no detriment to the employer`
              THEN `unless an exception applies` (`the work exception for` g w e) "s 54(3)" "s 54(3) itself (fork F2)"
              ELSE `not unlawful under s 54(3): the practice is not one the subsection protects (the text's no)`
    ELSE `the work answer for discrimination` g w (`the meaning of discrimination` g t) e

@export Was what my employer, or the employer I applied to, did unlawful discrimination under the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA) (ss 11, 35AC, 35B, 35P, 37, 54, 66B, 66W, 67B, with the exceptions in ss 11(3) to 35, 35M, 50 to 52, 54(4), 66, 66Q to 66ZS, 69, 72 and 73)? It is unlawful for an employer to discriminate against a job applicant (in the arrangements, the decision or the terms offered) or an employee (in terms, access to promotion, transfer, training or benefits, dismissal or other detriment), unless an exception applies; the employer must prove the exception (s 123).
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Ground` @desc The attribute you say you were treated badly for. One of: sex; marital status; pregnancy; breast feeding or bottle feeding; gender history; family responsibility or family status; sexual orientation; race; religious conviction; political conviction; impairment; age; publication of my details on the Fines Enforcement Registrar website
      `what was done` IS A `What was done` @desc What the employer did. As a job applicant: in the arrangements made for deciding who should be offered employment; in deciding who should be offered employment; in the terms or conditions on which employment was offered. As an employee: in the terms or conditions of my employment; by denying or limiting my access to promotion, transfer, training or other benefits of employment; by dismissing me; by subjecting me to any other detriment; by refusing me permission to carry out a religious practice during working hours
      `treated less favourably because of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you treated less favourably than a person without that attribute would be in the same or not materially different circumstances, because of your attribute or a characteristic generally belonging to or imputed to people with it? It is enough that it was one of the reasons
      `treated less favourably because of an associate's attribute` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you treated less favourably because of the attribute of a relative or associate of yours?
      `segregated because of race` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For race only: were you segregated from people of a different race because of race?
      `treated as being of my former sex` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For gender history only: were you treated as being of your former sex?
      `the less favourable treatment was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For pregnancy only: has it been found that the less favourable treatment was reasonable in the circumstances?
      `a guide dog or hearing dog` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For impairment only: are you blind, deaf, partially blind or partially deaf, and treated less favourably because of your guide dog or hearing dog?
      `a requirement or condition was imposed on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you required to comply with a requirement or condition (a rule, policy or practice)?
      `a substantially higher proportion of others comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do a substantially higher proportion of people without your attribute comply, or are able to comply, with it?
      `the requirement is not reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement or condition not reasonable in the circumstances (as found by the Tribunal, or as you put it)?
      `I do not or cannot comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you not comply, or are you not able to comply, with it?
      `I am a gender reassigned person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For gender history only: are you a gender reassigned person as s 4(1) defines it?
      `domestic duties where the employer lives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the job to perform domestic duties in the employer's own home (the premises or private household where the employer lives)?
      `the employer's number of employees` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people does the employer employ, not counting people employed to do domestic duties? (Matters for religious or political conviction only.)
      `being of the other sex is a genuine occupational qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For sex only: has the employer shown that being of the other sex is a genuine occupational qualification for the position (s 27(2): physical attributes other than strength or stamina, an acting role, fitting clothing, searches, entering lavatories or undress areas, living-in, or a position declared by regulation)?
      `the employer already has enough employees of the other sex for the duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For sex only: does the employer already have enough employees of the other sex who can do those duties and whom it would be reasonable to put on them (s 27(3))?
      `only rights given to women for pregnancy, childbirth or feeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a man complaining of sex discrimination: is the complaint only that the employer gave women rights or privileges in connection with pregnancy, childbirth, breast feeding or bottle feeding (s 28)?
      `the job is one of two for a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For marital status only: is the job one of 2 to be held by a married couple or a couple in a de facto relationship (s 29)?
      `a measure for equal opportunity or special needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a purpose of the act to ensure people with a particular attribute have equal opportunities, or to give them access to facilities, services or opportunities to meet their special needs (ss 31, 35K, 35ZD, 51, 66R, 66ZP), or, for family responsibility, to give people with it rights, benefits or privileges (s 35B(4))?
      `the duties involve caring for children where they live` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For sex or marital status: do the duties involve caring for a child or children in the place where they live (s 33)?
      `my spouse is meant to work for the employer too` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For marital status: is it intended that your spouse would also be employed by the same employer (s 33(2)(b))?
      `a likelihood of collusion with my relative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For family responsibility or family status: are you a relative of an employee (of this or another employer), and has the employer shown, after reasonable enquiries, a significant likelihood of collusion between you and that relative that would damage its business (s 35M)?
      `the work needs a particular race, impairment or age for authenticity or welfare services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For race, impairment or age: does the work involve a dramatic or other entertainment role, artist's or photographic modelling, or (race) serving food or drink, where a person of that race, impairment or age is required for authenticity, or providing welfare services that can most effectively be given by such a person (ss 50, 66S, 66ZQ)?
      `a religious school or religious health service, and religious duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For religious or political conviction: is the employer a private educational authority, or a religious body employing you in a hospital or health service, and do your duties involve religious observance or practice (s 66(1))?
      `a political job` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For political conviction: was the job offered as an electoral officer, ministerial adviser or officer, worker for a political party, member of someone's electoral staff, or similar (s 66(2))?
      `the employer reasonably concluded I could not do the work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For impairment, in deciding whom to employ or in dismissing: was it reasonable for the employer to conclude, on information it had taken reasonable steps to get, that because of the impairment you could not do the work reasonably required, or would need services or facilities causing it unjustifiable hardship (s 66Q(1))?
      `the terms are reasonable given my impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For impairment, in terms or conditions or access to benefits: are the terms reasonable having regard to the limitation your impairment imposes on doing the work, or the services or facilities you need (s 66Q(2))?
      `terms imposed for reasonable health and safety considerations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For age, in terms or conditions: were they imposed to comply with health and safety considerations that are reasonable in the circumstances (s 66ZM)?
      `an offer of a voluntary retirement or severance scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For age: is the complaint about being offered a voluntary phased-in retirement, voluntary retirement, retirement incentive, severance or like scheme (s 66ZN(1))?
      `necessary to comply with a youth wages provision or an older written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For age: was it necessary in order to comply with a youth wages or youth ratio provision (under 21) of an award, industrial agreement or the Minimum Conditions of Employment Act 1993, or a written law in force when Part IVB began (s 66ZS(1))?
      `necessary to comply with an order of the Tribunal or a court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it necessary for the employer to do it in order to comply with an order of the State Administrative Tribunal or of a court (s 69)?
      `a religious appointment or a religious body's practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the ordination or appointment of priests or ministers, selection of people for religious observance or practice, or an act of a body established for religious purposes that conforms to its doctrines or avoids injury to its adherents' religious susceptibilities (s 72)?
      `staff of a religious school, in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it about employment on the staff of a school or other educational institution run by the doctrines of a religion, and did the employer act in good faith to avoid injury to the religious susceptibilities of its adherents (s 73(1))?
      `recognised as necessary or desirable by my religion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a refused religious practice: is the practice of a kind recognised as necessary or desirable by people of your religion?
      `reasonable to do in working hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a refused religious practice: is doing it during working hours reasonable in the circumstances of your employment?
      `no detriment to the employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a refused religious practice: does it subject the employer to no detriment at all?
GIVETH A `Was it unlawful in work`
`ss 11 to 67B -- was what my employer did unlawful` `the ground` `what was done` `treated less favourably because of it` `treated less favourably because of an associate's attribute` `segregated because of race` `treated as being of my former sex` `the less favourable treatment was reasonable` `a guide dog or hearing dog` `a requirement or condition was imposed on me` `a substantially higher proportion of others comply` `the requirement is not reasonable` `I do not or cannot comply` `I am a gender reassigned person` `domestic duties where the employer lives` `the employer's number of employees` `being of the other sex is a genuine occupational qualification` `the employer already has enough employees of the other sex for the duties` `only rights given to women for pregnancy, childbirth or feeding` `the job is one of two for a couple` `a measure for equal opportunity or special needs` `the duties involve caring for children where they live` `my spouse is meant to work for the employer too` `a likelihood of collusion with my relative` `the work needs a particular race, impairment or age for authenticity or welfare services` `a religious school or religious health service, and religious duties` `a political job` `the employer reasonably concluded I could not do the work` `the terms are reasonable given my impairment` `terms imposed for reasonable health and safety considerations` `an offer of a voluntary retirement or severance scheme` `necessary to comply with a youth wages provision or an older written law` `necessary to comply with an order of the Tribunal or a court` `a religious appointment or a religious body's practice` `staff of a religious school, in good faith` `recognised as necessary or desirable by my religion` `reasonable to do in working hours` `no detriment to the employer` MEANS
    `the work answer` `the ground` `what was done` `the treatment` `the exceptions` `the practice`
    WHERE
        `the treatment` MEANS `The treatment` WITH
            `treated less favourably because of my attribute` IS `treated less favourably because of it`
            `treated less favourably because of an associate's attribute` IS `treated less favourably because of an associate's attribute`
            `segregated because of race` IS `segregated because of race`
            `treated as being of my former sex` IS `treated as being of my former sex`
            `the less favourable treatment was reasonable` IS `the less favourable treatment was reasonable`
            `a guide dog or hearing dog` IS `a guide dog or hearing dog`
            `a requirement or condition was imposed on me` IS `a requirement or condition was imposed on me`
            `a substantially higher proportion of others comply` IS `a substantially higher proportion of others comply`
            `the requirement is not reasonable` IS `the requirement is not reasonable`
            `I do not or cannot comply` IS `I do not or cannot comply`
            `I am a gender reassigned person` IS `I am a gender reassigned person`
        `the exceptions` MEANS `The exception facts` WITH
            `domestic duties where the employer lives` IS `domestic duties where the employer lives`
            `the employer's number of employees` IS `the employer's number of employees`
            `being of the other sex is a genuine occupational qualification` IS `being of the other sex is a genuine occupational qualification`
            `the employer already has enough employees of the other sex for the duties` IS `the employer already has enough employees of the other sex for the duties`
            `only rights given to women for pregnancy, childbirth or feeding` IS `only rights given to women for pregnancy, childbirth or feeding`
            `the job is one of two for a couple` IS `the job is one of two for a couple`
            `a measure for equal opportunity or special needs` IS `a measure for equal opportunity or special needs`
            `the duties involve caring for children where they live` IS `the duties involve caring for children where they live`
            `my spouse is meant to work for the employer too` IS `my spouse is meant to work for the employer too`
            `a likelihood of collusion with my relative` IS `a likelihood of collusion with my relative`
            `the work needs a particular race, impairment or age for authenticity or welfare services` IS `the work needs a particular race, impairment or age for authenticity or welfare services`
            `a religious school or religious health service, and religious duties` IS `a religious school or religious health service, and religious duties`
            `a political job` IS `a political job`
            `the employer reasonably concluded I could not do the work` IS `the employer reasonably concluded I could not do the work`
            `the terms are reasonable given my impairment` IS `the terms are reasonable given my impairment`
            `terms imposed for reasonable health and safety considerations` IS `terms imposed for reasonable health and safety considerations`
            `an offer of a voluntary retirement or severance scheme` IS `an offer of a voluntary retirement or severance scheme`
            `necessary to comply with a youth wages provision or an older written law` IS `necessary to comply with a youth wages provision or an older written law`
            `necessary to comply with an order of the Tribunal or a court` IS `necessary to comply with an order of the Tribunal or a court`
            `a religious appointment or a religious body's practice` IS `a religious appointment or a religious body's practice`
            `staff of a religious school, in good faith` IS `staff of a religious school, in good faith`
        `the practice` MEANS `The religious practice` WITH
            `recognised as necessary or desirable by my religion` IS `recognised as necessary or desirable by my religion`
            `reasonable to do in working hours` IS `reasonable to do in working hours`
            `no detriment to the employer` IS `no detriment to the employer`

§§ `ss 24 and 49A -- Was I harassed unlawfully at work?`

-- Where the person stands with the harasser. s 24(1): "It is unlawful for a person to harass sexually -- (a) an employee
-- of that or any other person; or (b) a person who is seeking employment by that or any other person." s 49A(1): "It is
-- unlawful for a person (... the harasser) to harass racially -- (a) an employee of the harasser; or (b) an employee of a
-- person by whom the harasser is employed; or (c) a person who is seeking employment by the harasser or by an employer of
-- the harasser."
DECLARE `Where I stand with the harasser` IS ONE OF
    `the harasser is my employer`
    `the harasser works for my employer too`
    `I was seeking work with the harasser or the harasser's employer`
    `I am an employee and the harasser is not my employer or a fellow employee`
    `I was seeking work with someone other than the harasser or the harasser's employer`

DECLARE `Was I harassed unlawfully` IS ONE OF
    `unlawful harassment` HAS `the provision` IS A STRING
    `not harassment as the Act defines it (the "if" is not met: the text's no)`
    `NOTHING-kind` HAS `why` IS A STRING

-- s 24(3): "A person shall ... be taken to harass sexually another person if the firstmentioned person makes an unwelcome
-- sexual advance, or an unwelcome request for sexual favours, to the other person, or engages in other unwelcome conduct
-- of a sexual nature in relation to the other person, and -- (a) the other person has reasonable grounds for believing
-- that a rejection of the advance, a refusal of the request or the taking of objection to the conduct would disadvantage
-- the other person in any way in connection with the other person's employment or work or possible employment or
-- possible work; or (b) as a result of the other person's rejection ... refusal ... or taking of objection ..., the other
-- person is disadvantaged in any way in connection with [that]". (4): conduct of a sexual nature includes a statement of
-- a sexual nature made to or in the presence of the person, orally or in writing.
@export Was I sexually harassed unlawfully at work or when seeking work, under the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA) (s 24(1), (3), (4))? Anyone who makes an unwelcome sexual advance, request for sexual favours or other unwelcome sexual conduct (including statements) towards an employee or job seeker harasses them if they reasonably believed objecting would disadvantage them at work, or they were disadvantaged because they objected.
GIVEN `where I stand` IS A `Where I stand with the harasser` @desc Where you stood with the person you say harassed you. One of: the harasser is my employer; the harasser works for my employer too; I was seeking work with the harasser or the harasser's employer; I am an employee and the harasser is not my employer or a fellow employee (for example a customer or client); I was seeking work with someone other than the harasser or the harasser's employer
      `unwelcome sexual conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person make an unwelcome sexual advance or an unwelcome request for sexual favours to you, or engage in other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature towards you (including a sexual statement about you, made to you or in your presence, spoken or written)?
      `I reasonably believed objecting would disadvantage me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have reasonable grounds for believing that rejecting, refusing or objecting would disadvantage you in any way in your employment or work, or possible employment or work?
      `I was disadvantaged because I objected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you disadvantaged in any way in your employment or work, or possible employment or work, because you rejected, refused or objected?
GIVETH A `Was I harassed unlawfully`
`s 24 -- was I sexually harassed unlawfully` `where I stand` `unwelcome sexual conduct` `I reasonably believed objecting would disadvantage me` `I was disadvantaged because I objected` MEANS
    IF      `unwelcome sexual conduct`
        AND (`I reasonably believed objecting would disadvantage me` OR `I was disadvantaged because I objected`)
    THEN IF     `where I stand` EQUALS `I was seeking work with the harasser or the harasser's employer`
             OR `where I stand` EQUALS `I was seeking work with someone other than the harasser or the harasser's employer`
         THEN `unlawful harassment` "s 24(1)(b): a person seeking employment by that or any other person"
         ELSE `unlawful harassment` "s 24(1)(a): an employee of that or any other person"
    ELSE `not harassment as the Act defines it (the "if" is not met: the text's no)`

-- s 49A(3): "A person shall ... be taken to harass racially another person if the firstmentioned person threatens,
-- abuses, insults or taunts the other person on a ground referred to in section 49D, and -- (a) the other person has
-- reasonable grounds for believing that objecting ... would disadvantage the other person in any way in connection with
-- the employment or work, or possible employment or possible work, of the other person; or (b) as a result of the
-- objection ..., the other person is disadvantaged in any way in connection with [that]". s 49D: the grounds are the
-- race, or a characteristic appertaining generally or generally imputed to persons of the race, of the person or of a
-- relative or associate of the person.
@export Was I racially harassed unlawfully at work or when seeking work, under the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA) (ss 49A(1), (3), 49D)? It covers threats, abuse, insults or taunts about your race (or a relative's or associate's) by your employer, a fellow employee, or a person you sought work with, where you reasonably believed objecting would disadvantage you at work, or you were disadvantaged because you objected.
GIVEN `where I stand` IS A `Where I stand with the harasser` @desc Where you stood with the person you say harassed you. One of: the harasser is my employer; the harasser works for my employer too; I was seeking work with the harasser or the harasser's employer; I am an employee and the harasser is not my employer or a fellow employee (for example a customer or client); I was seeking work with someone other than the harasser or the harasser's employer
      `threatened, abused, insulted or taunted about race` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person threaten, abuse, insult or taunt you on the ground of your race, or a relative's or associate's race (or a characteristic generally belonging to or imputed to people of that race)?
      `I reasonably believed objecting would disadvantage me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you have reasonable grounds for believing that objecting would disadvantage you in any way in your employment or work, or possible employment or work?
      `I was disadvantaged because I objected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you disadvantaged in any way in your employment or work, or possible employment or work, because you objected?
GIVETH A `Was I harassed unlawfully`
`s 49A -- was I racially harassed unlawfully` `where I stand` `threatened, abused, insulted or taunted about race` `I reasonably believed objecting would disadvantage me` `I was disadvantaged because I objected` MEANS
    IF      (NOT `threatened, abused, insulted or taunted about race`)
         OR (    (NOT `I reasonably believed objecting would disadvantage me`)
             AND (NOT `I was disadvantaged because I objected`))
    THEN `not harassment as the Act defines it (the "if" is not met: the text's no)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `where I stand`
         WHEN `the harasser is my employer` THEN `unlawful harassment` "s 49A(1)(a): an employee of the harasser"
         WHEN `the harasser works for my employer too` THEN `unlawful harassment` "s 49A(1)(b): an employee of a person by whom the harasser is employed"
         WHEN `I was seeking work with the harasser or the harasser's employer` THEN `unlawful harassment` "s 49A(1)(c): a person seeking employment by the harasser or by an employer of the harasser"
         OTHERWISE `NOTHING-kind` "s 49A(1) names only the harasser's own employees, fellow employees and job seekers; racial harassment by a customer, client or stranger is not within it (finding 4)"

§§ `s 67 -- Was I victimised?`

-- s 67(1): "It is unlawful for a person (... the victimiser) to subject, or threaten to subject, another person (... the
-- person victimised) to any detriment on the ground that the person victimised -- (a) has made, or proposes to make, a
-- complaint under this Act; or (b) has brought, or proposes to bring, proceedings ...; or (c) has furnished, or proposes
-- to furnish, any information, or has produced or proposes to produce, any documents to a person exercising or
-- performing any function under this Act; or (d) has appeared, or proposes to appear, as a witness before the Tribunal
-- ...; or (e) has reasonably asserted, or proposes to assert, any rights ... under this Act; or (f) has made an
-- allegation that a person has done an act that is unlawful by reason of a provision of Part II, IIAA, IIA, IIB, III, IV,
-- IVA, IVB or IVC, or on the ground that the victimiser believes that the person victimised has done, or proposes to do,
-- an act or thing referred to in any of paragraphs (a) to (f)." (2): "Subsection (1)(f) does not apply if it is proved
-- that the allegation was false and was not made in good faith." (3): failing to do the proposed thing, or withdrawing
-- or losing the complaint, does not affect s 67(1).
DECLARE `Was I victimised unlawfully` IS ONE OF
    `yes: unlawful victimisation (s 67(1))`
    `no: s 67(1)(f) does not apply, as the allegation was proved false and not made in good faith (s 67(2): the text's no)`
    `NOTHING-kind: s 67 forbids a detriment or threat on the listed grounds only; these facts are outside it`

@export Was I victimised unlawfully under the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA) (s 67)? It is unlawful to subject you, or threaten to subject you, to any detriment because you complained, brought proceedings, gave information or documents, were a witness, asserted rights under the Act, or alleged unlawful discrimination or harassment (or because someone believes you did or will). It still applies if you withdrew or lost the complaint.
GIVEN `I was subjected or threatened with a detriment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you subjected to a detriment, or threatened with one?
      `because of a complaint, proceedings, information, being a witness or asserting rights` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it because you made or proposed to make a complaint under the Act, brought or proposed to bring proceedings, gave or proposed to give information or documents to someone acting under the Act, appeared or proposed to appear as a witness before the Tribunal, or reasonably asserted or proposed to assert rights under the Act (or because the person believed you had or would)?
      `because I alleged unlawful discrimination or harassment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it because you alleged that someone had done an act unlawful under the discrimination or harassment Parts of the Act (or because the person believed you had or would)?
      `the allegation was proved false and not in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it been proved that your allegation was false and was not made in good faith?
GIVETH A `Was I victimised unlawfully`
`s 67 -- was I victimised` `I was subjected or threatened with a detriment` `because of a complaint, proceedings, information, being a witness or asserting rights` `because I alleged unlawful discrimination or harassment` `the allegation was proved false and not in good faith` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I was subjected or threatened with a detriment` AND `because of a complaint, proceedings, information, being a witness or asserting rights`
        THEN `yes: unlawful victimisation (s 67(1))`
        IF      `I was subjected or threatened with a detriment` AND `because I alleged unlawful discrimination or harassment`
            AND (NOT `the allegation was proved false and not in good faith`)
        THEN `yes: unlawful victimisation (s 67(1))`
        IF `I was subjected or threatened with a detriment` AND `because I alleged unlawful discrimination or harassment`
        THEN `no: s 67(1)(f) does not apply, as the allegation was proved false and not made in good faith (s 67(2): the text's no)`
        OTHERWISE `NOTHING-kind: s 67 forbids a detriment or threat on the listed grounds only; these facts are outside it`

§§ `ss 160, 161 -- Who is answerable to me?`

-- s 161(1): "Subject to subsection (2), where an employee or agent of a person does, in connection with the employment of
-- the employee or with the duties of the agent as an agent -- (a) an act that would, if it were done by the person, be
-- unlawful under this Act ...; or (b) an act that is unlawful under this Act, this Act applies in relation to that
-- person as if that person had also done the act." (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply ... if it is established that
-- the person took all reasonable steps to prevent the employee or agent from doing acts of the kind".
DECLARE `Is the employer answerable for its employee's act` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Act applies to the employer or principal as if it had also done the act (s 161(1))`
    `no: the employer or principal established that it took all reasonable steps to prevent acts of that kind (s 161(2): the text's no)`
    `no: the act was not done in connection with the employment or the agency (s 161(1)'s "where" is not met: the text's no)`

@export Is the employer (or principal) answerable for discrimination or harassment done to me by one of its employees or agents, under the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA) (s 161)? Yes, if the act was done in connection with the employment or agency and would be unlawful if the employer did it, unless the employer shows it took all reasonable steps to prevent acts of that kind.
GIVEN `the act would be unlawful if the employer did it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act one that is unlawful under the Act, or that would be unlawful if the employer or principal itself had done it?
      `done in connection with the employment or agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the employee or agent do it in connection with their employment, or their duties as agent?
      `the employer took all reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the employer or principal established that it took all reasonable steps to prevent its employees or agents from doing acts of that kind?
GIVETH AN `Is the employer answerable for its employee's act`
`s 161 -- is the employer answerable` `the act would be unlawful if the employer did it` `done in connection with the employment or agency` `the employer took all reasonable steps to prevent it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the act would be unlawful if the employer did it` AND `done in connection with the employment or agency`))
        THEN `no: the act was not done in connection with the employment or the agency (s 161(1)'s "where" is not met: the text's no)`
        IF `the employer took all reasonable steps to prevent it`
        THEN `no: the employer or principal established that it took all reasonable steps to prevent acts of that kind (s 161(2): the text's no)`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the Act applies to the employer or principal as if it had also done the act (s 161(1))`

-- s 160: "A person who causes, instructs, induces, aids, or permits another person to do an act that is unlawful under
-- this Act shall for the purposes of this Act be taken also to have done the act."
DECLARE `Is that person answerable too` IS ONE OF
    `yes: taken also to have done the act (s 160)`
    `NOTHING-kind: s 160 reaches only a person who caused, instructed, induced, aided or permitted the act`

@export Is a person who caused, instructed, encouraged, helped or allowed someone else to discriminate against or harass me answerable too, under the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA) (s 160)? Such a person is taken also to have done the unlawful act.
GIVEN `the act done to me is unlawful under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act done to you unlawful under the Act (for example, discrimination or harassment that the other questions found unlawful)?
      `the person caused, instructed, induced, aided or permitted it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that other person cause, instruct, induce, aid or permit the act?
GIVETH AN `Is that person answerable too`
`s 160 -- is that person answerable too` `the act done to me is unlawful under the Act` `the person caused, instructed, induced, aided or permitted it` MEANS
    IF `the act done to me is unlawful under the Act` AND `the person caused, instructed, induced, aided or permitted it`
    THEN `yes: taken also to have done the act (s 160)`
    ELSE `NOTHING-kind: s 160 reaches only a person who caused, instructed, induced, aided or permitted the act`
